      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Let's dive deeper. The pressure difference between the top and bottom of the wing is the primary driver of lift. Typically, 20-30% of lift is due to the pressure difference caused by Bernoulli's principle (when air speeds up over the curved surface), and the remaining 70-80% is due to the force exerted by Newton's third law (when air is pushed down by a force, resulting in an upward reaction). This pressure difference creates the upward force that counteracts the weight of the aircraft, allowing it to fly.",
